WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
BUKOLA AYODELE: Today, we're
talking about Google Cloud

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:02.700
Next.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.100
I'm Bakula, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.189
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.610
Google Cloud Next just happened
and it was quite an event.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.680
Hundreds of speakers
came from Google Cloud,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.200
and our partners came together
to talk about everything

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.750
from Anthos to Zero Trust.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.000
Don't worry if you didn't
get a chance to see it live.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.620
We have all the Talks
interactive sessions available,

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.220
so you can catch up on all
the exciting announcements.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.410
Here's a few of our favorites.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.030
Developing the Cloud
should help you

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.670
unlock new ways to work
without locking you in.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.273
There is no shortage of
conversation around Anthos,

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:36.690
and there's plenty
of new features

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.350
to help you take advantage
of all that Cloud offers.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.740
Anthos for virtual machines lets
you standardize on Kubernetes,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.080
even with virtual
machine workloads.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.420
And the Anthos
Multi-Cloud API will

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.290
make it easier to manage GKE
clusters running on other Cloud

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.550
providers.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.960
Good security comes from more
than just the tools available.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.600
It's about the knowledge
and best practices.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.180
The Google Cloud
Cybersecurity Action Team

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.069
gathers experts
from across Google

00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:07.530
to guide you through
security transformations

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.660
and to make your business safer.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.810
Of course, we also have tools
like data loss prevention built

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:15.420
into BigQuery to
identify sensitive data,

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.760
and expanding Security
Command Center

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.280
with Chronicle integration.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.980
Dealing with the data
can also be a challenge.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.050
Driving business
value can be difficult

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.650
if your teams are blocked on
how to collect or analyze data.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.750
Vertex AI is a
centralized solution

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:34.710
with integration across data
PROC, BigQuery, Dataplex,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.730
and Looker.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.270
Vertex AI Workbench offers
a unified user experience

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.430
for building and
deploying ML models.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.280
And serverless Spark
on Google Cloud

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.470
lets you focus on
what matters most

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.270
to your applications
and your data.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.700
Of course, we can't
have the Cloud

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.350
without protecting the Earth.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.000
That's why we're
excited to announce

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
that Google is committing to
running on carbon-free energy

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.560
by 2030.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.540
We're also launching
Carbon Footprint,

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.850
which helps you measure,
track, and report

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.010
on your sustainability goals.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.920
Active Assist is also being
updated with information

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.169
on carbon impact
for recommendations,

00:02:10.169 --> 00:02:12.330
and Earth Engine is
coming to Google Cloud

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.730
to bring you geospatial
data at scale.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.980
Wow, that's a lot
of announcements.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.570
If you want to read
more or see a full list,

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.770
check out the link.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.220
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.330
We'll see you in the Cloud.

